Z||000000||Ferrari_cdn||08-18-2001||08:55 PM||||Does a '84 2m4 with manual tranny have a good (hard) acceleration from a stopped position?  I know it is not a fast car, im only questioning its acceleration.  Also just wondering what its top speed is able to achieve, not that im gonna try to drive it at its maximum speed all the time.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>I've seen some cars with a bluish or a purplish headlights when seen from a distance, does the Fiero use the same socket that those lights uses?||||reg||1
Z||000001||Mach10||08-18-2001||09:00 PM||||Heya 'Pegger!<P>Firstly, I've driven a coupld of 4s. I'll say that they aren't the fastest in the world, but they aren't the slowest either. The motor isn't too strong, but then, the body's light. I'd say that with the manual 4.10 gears, it'd be on par with most commuter sedans around. Off the line, the Fiero will bite hard. Good traction. Most 4cyls that I've seen will leave rubber. My v6 won't. I attribute that to the gearing and the more weight on the 6. <BR>Don't worry so much about speed. If you want to go fast, drop a 3800SC into it  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>As for the lights, those "purple" ones are actually not lightbulbs, per-se. It's called a HID system. You can get tinted bulbs that mimic the effect, but I doubt that you'd be able to find an HID conversion for any reasonable amount of money. For decent looking lights, I'd recommend a Sylvania Cool Blue Halogen bulb. I always liked the light. Nice, cold white. Looks better than the typical "warm" yellowish or the irritatingly bright HIDs, IMO.||||reg||10
Z||000002||Ferrari_cdn||08-18-2001||09:31 PM||||  <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Most 4cyls that I've seen will leave rubber<HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Can I do that by just flooring the gas after the clutch is released and the Fiero moving slowly or would I have to keep the clutch in and rev it to 5000 or how high it should be and pop the clutch?  But Im worried that if I floored the pedal, the engine could go past redline and blow.  (I'm not that experienced when it comes to stick shifting)<P>edit:  Im aware that this could damage the tranny.  right?<p>[This message has been edited by Ferrari_cdn (edited 08-18-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000003||Jncomutt||08-18-2001||11:57 PM||||With my 84, I can take my foot slowly off the clutch, and while giving it no gas, it will not stall out.  It will idle around at about 1100 (bout 5mph)  If I put it to the floor from there, it spins em.  Also, I've gotten up to 110mph racing my friends Honda.  I think it could have gone 115 MAX but we ran out of road. <P>EDIT:  I'm not sure if its quite what your talking about but I got the headlight off of ebay for $37.  Theere is always a kit up for sale at any given time.  It came with 2 entirely new headlight encasements that allow for bulbs that can be interchanged thru the rear of the housing.  Also included were the 'Xenon Blue Bulbs' I think you maybe talking about.  They definatly do shine blue light.  (very visible when sitting behind white cars)<p>[This message has been edited by Jncomutt (edited 08-19-2001).]||||reg||1
